<!--
    A two-stage jump table whose byte map directly follows its table of
    4-byte offsets, in memory that is not read-only (Noelo-Lab/kuna#1669).

    Source: decompiler/crates/kuna-decomp/tests/fixtures/selector_domain.S,
    `gcc -c -DINPUT_COUNT=300`, `.text` loaded writable at 0x401000. The
    guarded index (300 values) reads a byte from the map, and the byte picks
    one of three rows. The map's values cannot be proven because it is
    writable, so the selector keeps all 256 values; rows 3 and up would be
    read from the map itself and from the bytes after it. The table ends at
    the first row that lies in the map, so only the three real rows remain.

    One pass, no option: a row read from the map's own bytes is false.
-->
